  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1210 PM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nThe next system to affect the area is currently moving across the \nIntermountain West and is expected to become a closed off low in the \nsouthwestern US by Friday afternoon. Models are in good agreement in \nshowing this system diving into northern Mexico which will take most \nof the large scale ascent south of the South Plains Saturday into \nSunday. An upper level jet streak will track from northern Mexico \ninto Far West Texas late on Friday then into Central Texas on \nSaturday. The northern edge of the large scale ascent will spread \nover the southern South Plains and southern Rolling Plains lasting \nfrom Saturday morning through Saturday evening. Cool surface \ntemperatures and a lack of instability will result in light \nstratiform precipitation during this time period. Dry weather is \nthen expected for the first half of next week with increasing \ntemperatures back up to seasonal averages.",
